%[text] ### Command-line Git
%[text] Some advanced capabilities of Git require a command-line version on your computer, but for light use, the version packaged with MATLAB is sufficient.
%[text] ![](text:image:3b47) **Try**. Run the command below to check if you have a command-line Git installed. 
!git
%[text] If you get information about how to use Git from this command, you already have a command-line Git installed. If you get a message 
%[text]  `'git' is not recognized as an internal or external command,`
%[text]  `operable program or batch file.`
%[text] then you do not have a command-line Git installed. You can follow instructions in the documentation to install a [command-line Git](https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/matlab_prog/set-up-git-source-control.html#mw_b5884d8b-7c3e-4c38-b055-28e39b604147).
%[text] Once you have installed and [configured Git](https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/matlab_prog/set-up-git-source-control.html) on your computer, you can use a local repository to track the changes you make to your code over time. You can also link to a remote repository hosted by GitHub or GitLab or many other options. 
